{#
  The 403 page for a Symfony-served route, rendered by App\Authorization\RouteGuard
  when a signed-in visitor is not allowed to reach a page.

  It replaces vendor/kokspflanze/bjy-authorize/view/error/403.phtml, which is what
  `error/403` still resolves to on the laminas side. Reproducing rather than reusing
  it is the point: bjy-authorize is abandoned and slated for retirement, and a
  ported page whose refusal comes out of that package would go blank the day it is
  removed. The wording and markup of the Route::ERROR branch are kept verbatim so
  the two front controllers say the same thing about the same page — everything else
  in that template (the Controller guard branch, the generic
  `error-unauthorized` branch) has no counterpart here: this guard raises exactly
  one kind of refusal.

  Rendered inside the shared layout, which is also where laminas puts it:
  BjyAuthorize\View\UnauthorizedStrategy adds the 403 ViewModel as a *child* of the
  layout's, so the page keeps its navbar, language chooser and footer.

  One deliberate difference: laminas leaves headTitle() untouched here, so the page
  is titled "Schoenstatt Link". This one says so.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>403 Forbidden</h1>
<p>
    You are not authorized to access {{ subject }}.
</p>
{% endblock %}
